From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader: EDEN_NX2_COMPOSE_GUARD keeps NaN and infinity out of the scene compose's pack

Core patch, on the T48 series. Off unless the switch is set. Aimed at the white flashes, but nothing yet
shows they come from this program.

Program a2fcaa95c5a162f2 is in the console's vulkan.bin of 6 Nov: the compose of Lichii issue 441, salt
bit flipped, 128 threads, and its code hashes to that value. Run through the recompiler off the console,
it is SMAA's neighbourhood blend, then a square root and a hand-written RGB9E5 pack. A thread does two
pixels, x and x + 8, unrolled, with no loop.

That changes the issue's story. A zero weight sum can't happen here: the reciprocal sits behind a 1e-05
gate on the largest weight, and the pair it sums holds that weight. All-zero weights take the plain copy
path. And the 125.0 was read as R11G11B10, which this word isn't.

What does break is the pack. It compares float bits as unsigned, so a NaN or infinity takes the shared
exponent. Replayed step by step: (0.4, 0.03, 0.04) comes back exact, a NaN channel reads 2.25 and the
others 0. One bad channel is red, green or blue, two are yellow, cyan or pink, three are white. Those are
the issue's colours and our white flashes. Where the NaN comes from isn't known: the colour image can
hold one, and a blend tap holding infinity gives 0 * inf.

In programs d9ee412f00ce399a and a2fcaa95c5a162f3, and any more in
EDEN_NX2_COMPOSE_GUARD_HASHES=<hex>,<hex>, a pixel with a float that is NaN, infinite or signed on its
way into the pack gets:
  EDEN_NX2_COMPOSE_GUARD=black  written as 0. Needs nothing from the target or the hardware.
  EDEN_NX2_COMPOSE_GUARD=1      not written. x moves out of the image: robustImageAccess, which RADV
                                leaves to the hardware, and no run has shown it. What stays in the pixel
                                was last drawn as R11G11B10, so it may read as the wrong colour.
  EDEN_NX2_COMPOSE_GUARD=mark   written green, to show where it fires. A compute program has no free
                                buffer to count skipped stores in, so this stands in for a count.

Each tested float has its own word at the end of local memory and each store reads only its own, three
each here, so the two pixels stay apart.

Hashes: these are of the lowered code, so they move if we lower a program differently from Lichii. The
low bit is the salt and is ignored. With the switch on, a compute program with floats on the way to a
store logs "Compose guard candidate", so a run names ours. d9ee412f00ce399a wasn't in that vulkan.bin,
its code is unread, and the guard may not fit it.

Cache: nothing to clear. vulkan.bin holds guest code, translated at every boot, and the driver's cache
keys on the SPIR-V, so guarded and plain programs can't mix.

Log, once per program built, and it proves the guard was applied, not that it fired:
  Compose guard black: shader a2fcaa95c5a162f2, workgroup 128x1x1, 2 image stores, 2 fed by floats,
  6 floats watched, 0 stores left alone

Not run on a PS5. The real program went through the real recompiler and guard off the console, and
spirv-val passes in all three modes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/compose_guard.h b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/compose_guard.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/compose_guard.h
@@ -0,0 +1,218 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+
+#pragma once
+
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <iterator>
+#include <optional>
+#include <string_view>
+#include <unordered_map>
+#include <unordered_set>
+#include <utility>
+#include <vector>
+
+#include "shader_recompiler/frontend/ir/ir_emitter.h"
+#include "shader_recompiler/frontend/ir/program.h"
+
+namespace Shader::Optimization {
+
+// EDEN_NX2_COMPOSE_GUARD: Ocarina's full-screen compose (Lichii issue 441) is SMAA's neighbourhood
+// blend, then a square root and a hand-written RGB9E5 pack that compares float bits as unsigned. A
+// NaN or infinity wins that compare and takes the shared exponent: its channel reads 1 to 2.25 and
+// the others fall to 0. One bad channel is pure red, green or blue, two are yellow, cyan or pink,
+// three are white. In the listed programs this stops such a pixel at the store:
+//   =1      it is not written
+//   =black  it is written as 0
+//   =mark   it is written green, to show where the guard fires
+// Any other value, or unset, changes nothing.
+//
+// A float that becomes integer bits on its way to a store is tested right there, into a word of its
+// own at the end of the program's local memory, and the store reads the words of its own data path.
+// The test's result can't be used directly: a value made in a branch doesn't dominate the store.
+// One flag for the whole thread won't do either: a thread covers two pixels, x and x + 8. A sign
+// counts as bad too: the pack handles unsigned colour only, and -0 is its brightest result.
+//
+// =1 drops a store by moving x out of the image, so no block is split and no phi moves. That is
+// defined with robustImageAccess, which RADV reports and leaves to the hardware. What stays in the
+// pixel may be in another encoding: the target was last drawn as R11G11B10.
+enum class ComposeGuardMode { Off, Skip, Black, Mark };
+
+inline ComposeGuardMode GetComposeGuardMode() {
+    static const ComposeGuardMode mode = [] {
+        const char* const text = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_COMPOSE_GUARD");
+        const std::string_view value = text != nullptr ? text : "";
+        return value == "1"       ? ComposeGuardMode::Skip
+               : value == "black" ? ComposeGuardMode::Black
+               : value == "mark"  ? ComposeGuardMode::Mark
+                                  : ComposeGuardMode::Off;
+    }();
+    return mode;
+}
+
+// The two hashes of issue 441, and EDEN_NX2_COMPOSE_GUARD_HASHES=<hex>,<hex>,... on top of them.
+inline const std::vector<u64>& ComposeGuardHashes() {
+    static const std::vector<u64> hashes = [] {
+        std::vector<u64> list{0xd9ee412f00ce399aULL, 0xa2fcaa95c5a162f3ULL};
+        const char* text = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_COMPOSE_GUARD_HASHES");
+        while (text != nullptr && *text != '\0') {
+            char* end = nullptr;
+            const u64 hash = std::strtoull(text, &end, 16);
+            if (end == text) {
+                ++text;
+                continue;
+            }
+            list.push_back(hash);
+            text = end;
+        }
+        return list;
+    }();
+    return hashes;
+}
+
+/// What ApplyComposeGuard found in one program.
+struct ComposeGuardEdits {
+    const char* what = "candidate"; ///< The mode, if the program was changed
+    size_t stores = 0;              ///< Image stores
+    size_t fed = 0;                 ///< Of those, with floats turned into bits in their data path
+    size_t watched = 0;             ///< Floats tested
+    size_t left = 0;                ///< Stores left alone
+};
+
+// The nearest floats a value is made from: walking back, a data path ends at its bitcast to bits.
+inline std::vector<IR::Inst*> ComposeGuardFloats(const IR::Value& root) {
+    std::vector<IR::Inst*> found;
+    std::unordered_set<const IR::Inst*> seen;
+    std::vector<IR::Value> pending{root};
+    while (!pending.empty()) {
+        const IR::Value value = pending.back();
+        pending.pop_back();
+        if (value.IsImmediate()) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        IR::Inst* const inst = value.InstRecursive();
+        if (!seen.insert(inst).second) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (inst->GetOpcode() == IR::Opcode::BitCastU32F32) {
+            found.push_back(inst);
+            continue;
+        }
+        for (size_t index = 0; index < inst->NumArgs(); ++index) {
+            pending.push_back(inst->Arg(index));
+        }
+    }
+    return found;
+}
+
+// With the switch on: nothing for a program that isn't listed and has no store fed by a float,
+// otherwise a line's worth of facts, so a run also names the programs that could be the compose.
+inline std::optional<ComposeGuardEdits> ApplyComposeGuard(IR::Program& program, u64 shader_hash) {
+    const ComposeGuardMode mode = GetComposeGuardMode();
+    if (mode == ComposeGuardMode::Off || program.stage != Stage::Compute) {
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    // The lowest bit is the native hash salt, as in ApplyOotVisualWorkaround.
+    const auto& hashes = ComposeGuardHashes();
+    const bool listed = std::any_of(hashes.begin(), hashes.end(), [shader_hash](u64 hash) {
+        return (shader_hash | 1) == (hash | 1);
+    });
+    struct Store {
+        IR::Block* block;
+        IR::Inst* inst;
+        std::vector<IR::Inst*> floats;
+    };
+    std::vector<Store> stores;
+    std::vector<std::pair<IR::Block*, IR::Inst*>> bitcasts;
+    for (IR::Block* const block : program.blocks) {
+        for (IR::Inst& inst : block->Instructions()) {
+            if (inst.GetOpcode() == IR::Opcode::BitCastU32F32) {
+                bitcasts.emplace_back(block, &inst);
+            } else if (inst.GetOpcode() == IR::Opcode::ImageWrite) {
+                stores.push_back(Store{block, &inst, ComposeGuardFloats(inst.Arg(2))});
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    ComposeGuardEdits edits;
+    edits.stores = stores.size();
+    edits.fed = static_cast<size_t>(std::count_if(
+        stores.begin(), stores.end(), [](const Store& store) { return !store.floats.empty(); }));
+    if (!listed) {
+        return edits.fed != 0 ? std::optional{edits} : std::nullopt;
+    }
+    edits.what = mode == ComposeGuardMode::Skip    ? "skip"
+                 : mode == ComposeGuardMode::Black ? "black"
+                                                   : "mark";
+    edits.left = stores.size() - edits.fed;
+
+    std::unordered_map<const IR::Inst*, u32> words;
+    const u32 first_word = (program.local_memory_size + 3) / 4;
+    u32 next_word = first_word;
+    for (const Store& store : stores) {
+        for (const IR::Inst* const value : store.floats) {
+            if (words.try_emplace(value, next_word).second) {
+                ++next_word;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    edits.watched = words.size();
+    if (words.empty()) {
+        return edits;
+    }
+    program.local_memory_size = next_word * 4;
+
+    // Local memory starts undefined. A phi has to stay at the head of its block.
+    IR::Block* const entry = program.blocks.front();
+    auto start = entry->begin();
+    while (start != entry->end() && start->GetOpcode() == IR::Opcode::Phi) {
+        ++start;
+    }
+    IR::IREmitter entry_ir{*entry, start};
+    for (u32 word = first_word; word < next_word; ++word) {
+        entry_ir.WriteLocal(entry_ir.Imm32(word), entry_ir.Imm32(0U));
+    }
+    for (const auto& [block, inst] : bitcasts) {
+        const auto word = words.find(inst);
+        if (word == words.end()) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        IR::IREmitter ir{*block, std::next(block->Instructions().iterator_to(*inst))};
+        const IR::U1 bad =
+            ir.IGreaterThanEqual(IR::U32{IR::Value{inst}}, ir.Imm32(0x7f800000U), false);
+        ir.WriteLocal(ir.Imm32(word->second),
+                      IR::U32{ir.Select(bad, ir.Imm32(1U), ir.Imm32(0U))});
+    }
+    for (const Store& store : stores) {
+        const IR::Value coords = store.inst->Arg(1);
+        const IR::Type coords_type = coords.Type();
+        if (store.floats.empty() ||
+            (mode == ComposeGuardMode::Skip && coords_type != IR::Type::U32x2 &&
+             coords_type != IR::Type::U32x3 && coords_type != IR::Type::U32x4)) {
+            edits.left += store.floats.empty() ? 0 : 1;
+            continue;
+        }
+        IR::IREmitter ir{*store.block, store.block->Instructions().iterator_to(*store.inst)};
+        IR::U32 any = ir.Imm32(0U);
+        for (const IR::Inst* const value : store.floats) {
+            any = ir.BitwiseOr(any, ir.LoadLocal(ir.Imm32(words.at(value))));
+        }
+        const IR::U1 hit = ir.INotEqual(any, ir.Imm32(0U));
+        if (mode == ComposeGuardMode::Skip) {
+            store.inst->SetArg(1, ir.CompositeInsert(coords,
+                                                     ir.Select(hit, ir.Imm32(0xffffffffU),
+                                                               ir.CompositeExtract(coords, 0)),
+                                                     0));
+        } else {
+            // Green 1.0 as RGB9E5 of its square root. Only that format reads as green.
+            const u32 word = mode == ComposeGuardMode::Mark ? 0x80020000U : 0U;
+            const IR::Value color = store.inst->Arg(2);
+            store.inst->SetArg(2, ir.CompositeInsert(color,
+                                                     ir.Select(hit, ir.Imm32(word),
+                                                               ir.CompositeExtract(color, 0)),
+                                                     0));
+        }
+    }
+    return edits;
+}
+
+} // namespace Shader::Optimization
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #include "shader_recompiler/frontend/maxwell/control_flow.h"
 #include "shader_recompiler/frontend/maxwell/translate_program.h"
 #include "shader_recompiler/ir_opt/passes.h"
+#include "shader_recompiler/ir_opt/compose_guard.h"
 #include "shader_recompiler/ir_opt/oot_visual_workaround.h"
 #include "shader_recompiler/program_header.h"
 #include "video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h"
@@ -2006,6 +2007,16 @@ std::unique_ptr<ComputePipeline> PipelineCache::CreateComputePipeline(
                     *oot_fog_sun, key.unique_hash, edits->compares, edits->gathers, edits->plain,
                     edits->sparse);
     }
+    // EDEN_NX2_COMPOSE_GUARD, compose_guard.h. Programs are translated at every boot and the
+    // driver's cache keys on the SPIR-V: no new cache either way.
+    if (const auto guard = Shader::Optimization::ApplyComposeGuard(program, key.unique_hash)) {
+        LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan,
+                    "Compose guard {}: shader {:016x}, workgroup {}x{}x{}, {} image stores, {} "
+                    "fed by floats, {} floats watched, {} stores left alone",
+                    guard->what, key.unique_hash, program.workgroup_size[0],
+                    program.workgroup_size[1], program.workgroup_size[2], guard->stores, guard->fed,
+                    guard->watched, guard->left);
+    }
     const VkDriverIdKHR driver_id = device.GetDriverID();
     const bool needs_shared_mem_clamp =
         driver_id == VK_DRIVER_ID_QUALCOMM_PROPRIETARY ||
